\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Jesus, if still the same Thou art,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  If all Thy promises are sure,
\par  Set up Thy kingdom in my heart,
\par  And make me rich, for I am poor:
\par  To me be all Thy treasures given,
\par  The kingdom of an inward heaven.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Thou hast pronounced the mourners blest;
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj  And lo, for Thee I ever mourn:
\par  I cannot: No! I will not rest,
\par  Till Thou, my only rest, return,
\par  Till Thou, the Prince of Peace, appear,
\par  And I receive the Comforter.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Where is the blessedness bestowed
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  On all that hunger after Thee?
\par  I hunger now, I thirst for God;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 See the poor fainting sinner, see.
\par And satisfy the endless peace,
\par And fill me with Thy righteousness.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Ah, Lord! If Thou art in that sigh,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Then hear Thyself within me pray;
\par Hear in my heart Thy Spirit's cry,
\par Mark what my labouring soul would say;
\par Answer the deep unuttered groan,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj   And show that Thou and I are one.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Shine on Thy work, disperse the gloom,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Light in Thy light I then shall see;
\par Say to my soul: Thy light is come,
\par Glory divine is risen on thee,
\par Thy warfare's past, thy mourning's o'er,
\par \pard      Look up, for thou shalt weep no more!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

